# Regenerable output from the falsification scripts.
#
# What stays in git: the scripts (~340 kB) and the per-frame result JSON
# (~340 kB). The JSON is kept deliberately -- it lets anyone re-analyse a run
# without repeating the fit, which costs about 25 minutes per arm.
#
# What is excluded: renders and intermediate arrays, which any script here
# rebuilds on demand and which total roughly 14 MB.
#
# NOTE ON LICENCE: renders/ contains direct projections of the 7-iron mesh.
# research/silhouette_poc/meshes/SOURCES.md admits that model for local research
# use only, with "neither the STL nor its normalized NPZ may be committed" and
# only "provenance, hash, attribution, and aggregate evaluation results" entering
# the repository. A render of the geometry is not an aggregate result, so it stays
# out of git along with the asset itself.

renders/
*.npy
*.log

# base64 staging for the artifact page
_*.txt
